From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: windowscodecs: half and float pixel formats, and conversions to and from them

64bppRGBAHalf, 64bppPRGBAHalf, 64bppRGBHalf and 48bppRGBHalf had no pixel
format info, so CreateComponentInfo failed for them; Paint.NET asks for
64bppPRGBAHalf when it draws its layer list.

The default format converter now converts to and from 64bppPRGBA,
64bppRGBAHalf, 64bppPRGBAHalf, 128bppRGBAFloat and 128bppPRGBAFloat. It goes
through premultiplied floats. The float and half formats hold linear
(scRGB) values and the integer ones are sRGB coded, so crossing between
them converts the gamma, as WIC's documented behavior is.

Gate: test/wuicomp-gate.sh.
